#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:23
#: 99a47c8c3dbb4c59b3f1d1b81a6e9420
msgid "It is based on the filter equations derived `here <https://github.com/priseborough/InertialNav/blob/master/derivations/RotationVectorAttitudeParameterisation/GenerateNavFilterEquations.m>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:26
#: 8be53ec468304eaf8fe4b6532aaf9f6a
msgid "EKF2 Advantages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:28
#: 20e7b5f55b2a441984b8ce44051705c8
msgid "It can run a separate EKF2 for each IMU making recovery from an IMU fault much more likely"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:29
#: 55e24591a1ca421880317bcd2f583697
msgid "It can switch between magnetometers if there is fault"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:30
#: 76a22053ce654278a1ca81940e368e1b
msgid "It can estimate gyro scale factors which can improve accuracy during high rate manoeuvres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:31
#: 6c975968d1a24f5497720451145894e9
msgid "It can simultaneously estimate both gyro offsets and orientation on startup whilst moving and doesn't rely on the DCM algorithm for its initial orientation. This makes it ideal for flying from moving platforms when the gyro has not been calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:32
#: 8a3b1adbfb9c41b5858d710ef58f4126
msgid "It can handle larger gyro bias changes in flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:33
#: 1566d897c2d144cab6bd3b4741736d68
msgid "It is able to recover faster from bad sensor data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:34
#: 2305c1fd2c324c5f9e0a69ed2c8cab24
msgid "It provides a slightly smoother output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:35
#: bdecb1e4dbfc4ed5ac000ae60f56a7e4
msgid "It is slightly more accurate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:36
#: f0903e45cb8042f9995f6ae13751ec9d
msgid "It uses slightly less computing power"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:37
#: 007b83a37af64346b365b3f51d099159
msgid "It starts using GPS when checks pass rather than waiting for the vehicle motors to arm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:41
#: 445575b8dae54189917f718dd20a5775
msgid "How does it achieve this?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:43
#: 62888b7fc3af4f65ac742aa36664bf8e
msgid "Instead of trying to estimate the quaternion orientation directly, it estimates an error rotation vector and applies the correction to the quaternion from the inertial navigation equations. This is better when there are large angle errors as it avoids errors associated with linearising quaternions across large angle changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:49
#: 25c5570e9a6345349c372c1ba2a72d44
msgid "See \"Rotation Vector in Attitude Estimation\", Mark E. Pittelkau, Journal of Guidance, Control, and Dynamics, 2003” for details on this approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:53
#: 544830a9f51648c8a46182dbb7134f6b
msgid "The new EKF runs on a delayed time horizon so that when measurements are fused, they are done so using the measurement, filter states and covariance matrix from the same point in time. The legacy EKF uses a simpler method where delayed measurements are fused using delayed states but the covariance matrix is from the current time which reduces accuracy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:60
#: b49c581a93dd476d8e4237c926f7325b
msgid "The delayed filter states are then predicted forward into the current time horizon using a complementary filter that removes the time delay and also filters out the sudden changes in the states that occur when measurements are fused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:64
#: 5ed184a5bee94999a2b1e45803cc3184
msgid "This approach was inspired by the output predictor work done by Ali Khosravian from ANU. \"Recursive Attitude Estimation in the Presence of Multi-rate and Multi-delay Vector Measurements,” A Khosravian, J Trumpf, R Mahony, T Hamel - American Control Conference, vol.-, 2015."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:69
#: 88aa56fd36bc4ff798c5036a7aa6dc76
msgid "This is computationally much cheaper than winding the states forward using buffered IMU data at each update, but slightly less accurate. The legacy EKF smooths the state corrections by applying them incrementally across the time to the next measurement which reduces stability of the filter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:75
#: e1dfad3a04b848f5b66f0e97df8a939e
msgid "Further optimisation of mathematics and code to improve speed have been introduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:77
#: 3d993c2e08a64eed866203c2c079fabd
msgid "A simple compass yaw angle fusion method with fixed declination has been added which is used on the ground or when magnetic interference prevents use of the more accurate 3-axis 6-state magnetometer fusion technique."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:83
#: d7b009f7e2e0417db1c03f10bb2bd0ca
msgid "Using EKF2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:85
#: d3598941c8ce4108965827ccd7e327c7
msgid "Enable the new EKF by setting EK2_ENABLE = 1.  EKF2 will now be running in parallel and logging, etc but it will not be used by the control loops."
