#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:294
#: 4db5cbdc12bc49d7af3a74f403fbe263
msgid "The EKF2 parameters have been tuned to provide a compromise between accuracy and robustness to sensor errors. it is likely that further improvements in performance are available with further tuning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:298
#: d8c154de9b694e8e8f32cd8a139471a8
msgid "If you have a question regarding tuning of the filer, please post `on the forums <https://discuss.ardupilot.org/>`__ along with your log file and mention the term EKF2 in your post title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:301
#: a406df8951954182bea681095a532ca9
msgid "The parameters for the new EKF start with the prefix EK2\\_ and are listed below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:304
#: 580a69af9b1544afa1c33ce03813c377
msgid "**EK2_ENABLE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:306
#: 6241e25b56704b759e61f3ccefee4daa
msgid "This turns the EKF 2 on and off. Set to 1 to turn on and 0 to turn off. Turning EKF2 on only makes the calculations run, it does not mean it will be used for flight control. To use it for flight control set AHRS_EKF_TYPE=2. A reboot or restart will need to be performed after changing the value of EK2_ENABLE for it to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:312
#: 9e49fe67ce434792b781687a95e52b7f
msgid "**EK2_GPS_TYPE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:314
#: f20aa7aa89db49568ef07e5699835e2d
msgid "This controls the use of GPS measurements :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:316
#: e3cd7f2b307e487c9e0c2634062b6083
msgid "0 = use 3D velocity & 2D position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:317
#: fbfc70a5d1b140b89e5ffd4e69d87e10
msgid "1 = use 2D velocity and 2D position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:318
#: 656848f7ef174435baac70a8a05f32ad
msgid "2 = use 2D position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:319
#: 5721ccd217c5436098da80ba70839d1c
msgid "3 = use no GPS (optical flow will be used if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:321
#: acc172cbddeb40f1a4da2a482061b77a
msgid "**EK2_VELNE_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:323
#: 7b14980fc441455c98905b55f7598b06
msgid "This sets a lower limit on the speed accuracy reported by the GPS receiver that is used to set horizontal velocity observation noise. If the model of receiver used does not provide a speed accuracy estimate, then the parameter value will be used. Increasing it reduces the weighting of the GPS horizontal velocity measurements. It has units of metres/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:330
#: aec6ba0e7c08436899ef1f969078baeb
msgid "**EK2_VELD_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:332
#: 4199050cb9de4acfb247d91784a15ad3
msgid "This sets a lower limit on the speed accuracy reported by the GPS receiver that is used to set vertical velocity observation noise in. If the model of receiver used does not provide a speed accuracy estimate, then the parameter value will be used. Increasing it reduces the weighting of the GPS vertical velocity measurements. It has units of metres/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:339
#: d005ca286b5f4c67917ecacd6a7bdf0c
msgid "**EK2_VEL_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:341
#: 980e9d8d0a1140c6885c8eae9d1e8c4b
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the GPS velocity measurement innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:346
#: 5def2c3fbee24ab59c9d857efe9ea5b3
msgid "**EK2_POSNE_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:348
#: ab21254effb1493682944ddc30e853c9
msgid "This sets the GPS horizontal position observation noise. Increasing it reduces the weighting of GPS horizontal position measurements. It has units of metres"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:352
#: 9cc06b04f0b84cdda0d9f486ca6bd635
msgid "**EK2_POS_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:354
#: 12a093b9c9334a63a93933925cf64a26
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the GPS position measurement innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:359
#: ff997f00caae401695580d64501eb40d
msgid "**EK2_GLITCH_RAD**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:361
#: 1974e90928bd42ce9ebd207ce2e01d9c
msgid "This controls the maximum radial uncertainty in position between the value predicted by the filter and the value measured by the GPS before the filter position and velocity states are reset to the GPS. Making this value larger allows the filter to ignore larger GPS glitches but also means that non-GPS errors such as IMU and compass can create a larger error in position before the filter is forced back to the GPS position. It has units of metres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:369
#: 069227971a434defa0a21791a0178472
msgid "**EK2_GPS_DELAY**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:371
#: 87d7e8fdd46245c4b4e53e2e9a81455f
msgid "This is the number of msec that the GPS measurements lag behind the inertial measurements. The maximum delay that can be compensated by the filter is 250 msec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:375
#: 5d748858d1714b95817b2b0f3d7e3b9c
msgid "**EK2_ALT_SOURCE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:377
#: 443af12283f942c48fd56ff9fd891a0d
msgid "This parameter controls which height sensor is used by the EKF. If the selected option cannot be used, it will default to Baro as the primary height source. Setting 0 will use the baro altitude at all times. Setting 1 uses the range finder and is only available in combination with optical flow navigation (EK2_GPS_TYPE = 3). Setting 2 uses GPS. When height sources other than Baro are in use, the offset between the Baro height and EKF height estimate is continually updated. If a switch to Baro height needs to be made when the filter is operating, then the  Baro height is corrected for the learned offset to prevent a sudden step in height estimate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:388
#: c86a47ef86224c8ba8ebce2610c45464
msgid "**EK2_ALT_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:390
#: b6a447e9569f414db5377387189584cb
msgid "This is the RMS value of noise in the altitude measurement. Increasing it reduces the weighting of the baro measurement and will make the filter respond more slowly to baro measurement errors, but will make it more sensitive to GPS and accelerometer errors.  It has units of metres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:395
#: cb19335f9d984f9b829df6e41057aafe
msgid "**EK2_HGT_I_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:397
#: fcc81856c0c747dba811306465f650bd
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the height measurement innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:402
#: a424f44293174e30a60ad4dcbc70c301
msgid "**EK2_HGT_DELAY**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:404
#: 841a3ce7d06d401fbc4e654995bd4217
msgid "This is the number of msec that the height measurements lag behind the inertial measurements. The maximum delay that can be compensated by the filter is 250 msec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:408
#: 9e02aa9529324597b066345cb9771401
msgid "**EK2_MAG_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:410
#: 65135bf1b8d949578195c9fa8ff115c3
msgid "This is the RMS value of noise in magnetometer measurements. Increasing it reduces the weighting on these measurements. It has units of mGauss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:413
#: e68a940107ab4585a2db14e194a2e4f6
msgid "**EK2_MAG_CAL**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:415
#: de5f13a57b004d9fa6d1a0c0beb2c5dd
msgid "This determines when the filter will use the 3-axis magnetometer fusion model that estimates both earth and body fixed magnetic field states. This model is only suitable for use when the external magnetic field environment is stable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:420
#: 5310a0aa40494de6acc74387da3308e9
msgid "EKF_MAG_CAL = 0 enables calibration when airborne and is the default setting for Plane users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:422
#: 6f1ba064d5f142a0b3fa48afc841a502
msgid "EKF_MAG_CAL = 1 enables calibration when manoeuvreing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:423
#: c5a2f3b401304705a1a4c28d3d086bd4
msgid "EKF_MAG_CAL = 2 prevents magnetometer calibration regardless of flight condition, is recommended if the external magnetic field is varying and is the default for rovers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:426
#: 5c6505f067d64efa8fd9ba3c0f1bde3e
msgid "EKF_MAG_CAL = 3 enables calibration when the first in-air field and yaw reset has completed and is the default for copters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:428
#: 1e50a346c69748d383ef2f40dd45328b
msgid "EKF_MAG_CAL = 4 enables calibration all the time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:430
#: ab59239738d6496db75b0935daa47f06
msgid "**EK2_MAG_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:432
#: a158bb8a248e4b31a7e49a65c980dcfd
msgid "This parameter sets the number of standard deviations applied to the magnetometer measurement innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:437
#: 75027fe1c6764cc2857bed46d9ca1470
msgid "**EK2_EAS_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:439
#: 6dd5a3de6fb94cf1b905460c867076cc
msgid "This is the RMS value of noise in equivalent airspeed measurements used by planes. Increasing it reduces the weighting of airspeed measurements and will make wind speed estimates less noisy and slower to converge. Increasing also increases navigation errors when dead-reckoning without GPS measurements. It has units of metres/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:445
#: 37c01f201cf24dc482244621a16be227
msgid "**EK2_EAS_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:447
#: 68dde351c75f4360a16e8fa8f01faa5e
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the airspeed measurement innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:452
#: ae016e198fe5441c8b1b02631f6b4847
msgid "**EK2_RNG_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:454
#: 544bb6ceca9b4c949769fcffe3721565
msgid "This is the RMS value of noise in the range finder measurement. Increasing it reduces the weighting on this measurement. It has units of metres."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:458
#: 0d445594608c4a1aa8805c27684952f6
msgid "**EK2_RNG_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:460
#: 50418eb942724b4794c2e7403fa53648
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the range finder innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:465
#: 039039100b07411086db519e22d8a5ed
msgid "**EK2_MAX_FLOW**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:467
#: 8060c37848624529a7ccf3afe184bac4
msgid "This parameter sets the magnitude maximum optical flow rate in that will be accepted by the filter. It has units of rad/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:470
#: 22f02df0275a4391ac6616071db8de42
msgid "**EK2_FLOW_NOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:472
#: c1bc620a599745e78e9b37eafd70e959
msgid "This is the RMS value of noise and errors in optical flow measurements. Increasing it reduces the weighting on these measurements. It has units of rad/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:476
#: 111b7ca00a7c4741bbdfa16ae1025c11
msgid "**EK2_FLOW_GATE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:478
#: d0aa7828319742b6a2beb0d55b9f372c
msgid "This sets the number of standard deviations applied to the optical flow innovation consistency check. Decreasing it makes it more likely that good measurements will be rejected. Increasing it makes it more likely that bad measurements will be accepted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:483
#: e92a415a7e08446c82639f6af54a817d
msgid "**EK2_FLOW_DELAY**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:485
#: 1dc02e8ab0bd4ad38674d664bb5d6580
msgid "This is the number of msec that the optical flow measurements lag behind the inertial measurements. It is the time from the end of the optical flow averaging period and does not include the time delay due to the 100msec of averaging within the flow sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:490
#: c35288f9b9b743129aaa408e5825073e
msgid "**EK2_GYRO_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:492
#: 29bfce1a65c94a0cb815215bbb0472db
msgid "This control disturbance noise controls the growth of estimated error due to gyro measurement errors excluding bias. Increasing it makes the filter trust the gyro measurements less and other measurements more. It has units of rad/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:497
#: cb207a6a0bc043c9bd187b554ccddf73
msgid "**EK2_ACC_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:499
#: d55f15c063374e49b4b32ce7dec995e2
msgid "This control disturbance noise controls the growth of estimated error due to accelerometer measurement errors excluding bias. Increasing it makes the filter trust the accelerometer measurements less and other measurements more. It has units of metres/sec/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:504
#: 639bc7c643ff4129a8135e0881631890
msgid "**EK2_GBIAS_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:506
#: d8f15211f88c41f3833a9e6682dc35ea
msgid "This state process noise controls the growth of the gyro delta angle bias state error estimates. Increasing it makes rate gyro bias estimation faster and noisier. It has units of rad/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:510
#: 4845cf5e41de424dbc182914cfb08d56
msgid "**EKF2_GSCL_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:512
#: a95569b29e284b298e289e3b5fbc0cf3
msgid "This state process noise controls the rate of gyro scale factor learning. Increasing it makes rate gyro scale factor estimation faster and noisier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:516
#: 7d66fab09de84689ac26ad62c13c1a80
msgid "**EK2_ABIAS_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:518
#: c0062a684ec7460a9b7e2798beb2f95e
msgid "This state process noise controls the growth of the vertical accelerometer delta velocity bias state error estimate. Increasing it makes accelerometer bias estimation faster and noisier. It has units of metres/sec/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:523
#: 8401d2f583e74e2988254a9e2bc5bf32
msgid "**EK2_MAG_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:525
#: 2c402fdc136a4e33b55c371056e2fcae
msgid "This state process noise controls the growth of magnetic field state error estimates. Increasing it makes magnetic field bias estimation faster and noisier. It has units of Gauss/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:529
#: 2a9aee2d29e74474bbc199b8398a2f4e
msgid "**EK2_WIND_PNOISE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:531
#: b8c75da6c4244304bd1ef520edecc40f
msgid "This state process noise controls the growth of wind state error estimates. Increasing it makes wind estimation faster and noisier. It has units of metres/sec/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:535
#: 6ea122c4016841be8da0b241bf5a69e1
msgid "**EK2_WIND_PSCALE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:537
#: bcca790718124c128557ab0e2a4a859d
msgid "This controls how much the process noise on the wind states is increased when gaining or losing altitude to take into account changes in wind speed and direction with altitude. Increasing this parameter increases how rapidly the wind states adapt when changing altitude, but does make wind velocity estimates noisier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:543
#: 1cc331069ad94aa8b64bf1877218542d
msgid "**EK2_GPS_CHECK**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:545
#: 34ea65fc0b07481b80ebbd1f7c17c479
msgid "This is a 1 byte bitmap controlling which GPS preflight checks are performed. Set to 0 to bypass all checks. Set to 255 perform all checks. Set to 3 to check just the number of satellites and HDoP. Set to 31 for the most rigorous checks that will still allow checks to pass when the copter is moving, eg launch from a boat. Setting a 1 in the following bit locations causes the corresponding checks to be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:552
#: c977990dd5064f539ba3350c556806f9
msgid "0: The receivers reported number of satellites must be >= 6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:554
#: 9eb54ac3a4dc41d5b2015f2e434fe8f2
msgid "1: The receivers reported HDoP must be >=2.5"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:556
#: 886aa36e422a46fc8c0adbeb8a30b759
msgid "2: The receivers reported speed accuracy must be less than1.0 metres/sec (if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:559
#: c03b5f843d41475b860516a3fa3c2ad1
msgid "3: The receivers reported horizontal position accuracy must be less than 5.0 metres (if available)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:562
#: ec0a9959563641b5acb49be8106a10f7
msgid "4: The EKF2 magnetometer or compass innovation consistency checks must be passing. If these checks are failing, then the yaw estimate is unreliable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:566
#: a263b3becb834071a2c77dae989a41e0
msgid "5: The rate of drift in the receivers reported horizontal position must be less than 0.3 metres/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:569
#: 4a9870e64d1646c9829de7a76d5ba50e
msgid "6: The receivers reported vertical speed after filtering must be less than 0.3 metres/sec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:572
#: 9472d6f936a3448f9230cd73237d8319
msgid "7: The receivers reported horizontal speed after filtering must be less than 0.3 metres/sec."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:575
#: d22cc9f6f07244989dc6897b975be5f6
msgid "Note: An unbroken pass on all selected checks for 10 seconds is required for the EKF2 to set its origin and start using GPS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:578
#: ea28855f3412467a9cc08173b6cf35a8
msgid "Note: The accuracy required for checks 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 can be adjusted using the EK2_CHECK_SCALE parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:581
#: 1e43ad8b4f924e778a882fcdddd87504
msgid "**EK2_CHECK_SCALE**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:583
#: 79566aa36e9240a7b175cd28fdbd5457
msgid "This is a percentage scaler applied to the thresholds that are used to check GPS accuracy before it is used by the EKF. Values greater than 100 increase and values less than 100 reduce the maximum GPS error the EKF will accept. This modifies the checks enabled by bits 2, 3, 5, 6 and 7 in the EK2_GPS_CHECK parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:589
#: 455fae0c2d8340819538b64be442bc68
msgid "**EK2_IMU_MASK**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:591
#: 166905c9234a4e3292db47073416068d
msgid "This is a 1 byte bitmap controlling which IMUs will be used by EKF2. A separate instance of EKF2 will be started for each IMU selected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:594
#: 64b0d6daf27d4082a001224d56d47f46
msgid "Set to 1 to use the first IMU only (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:595
#: 44a6310a0d0642ffb3ed0b03ba49b667
msgid "Set to 2 to use the second IMU only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:596
#: 61fa78241dff4290914e0cca66183e85
msgid "Set to 3 to use the first and second IMU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:598
#: 08e40f3a916d4892b4414f92d37de323
msgid "Additional IMU's up to a maximum of 6 can be used if memory and processing resources permit. There may be insufficient memory and processing resources to run multiple instances. If this occurs EKF2 will fail to start and the following message will be sent to the GCS console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf2-estimation-system.rst:607
#: 0a89b8988fe941b9ac847d2a9d3be9d0
msgid "If terrain data is not being used, some additional memory can be released by setting TERRAIN_ENABLE=0 and rebooting."
msgstr ""
